COMPILATION OF: E49G1

D: Disk Print
L: List Source Program

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 1

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 2

PL/I-80 V1.4 COMPILATION OF: E49G1

   1 a 0000 E49G1:
   2 a 0006   procedure options(main);
   3 a 0006   /* [E2E-49/P4] ORDERED relation `< ' with member LEFT, literal
   4 a 0006      RIGHT, EQUAL attributes (char(3) vs 'ABC').  [C346] measured
   5 a 0006      the relation family on QUALIFIED member pairs only; a literal
   6 a 0006      operand in a relation has NO object.  `<' is written-order per
   7 a 0006      the ORDER law, so H-A-sw and H-A-or predict the SAME staged
   8 a 0006      template `21 *D / EB / 21 *D(pool)'; the discriminator is the
   9 a 0006      equal-attribute COLLAPSE ([C342], keyed on the numbers, not
  10 a 0006      the relation): 06 03 / 78 vs two immediates 06 03 / 3E 03.
  11 a 0006      Strict skips JNC d2. */
  12 c 0006   dcl
  13 c 0006     1 rec,
  14 c 0006       2 na char(3),
  15 c 0006       2 nb char(3),
  16 c 0006       2 s2 char(2);
  17 c 0006   dcl k fixed bin(15);
  18 c 0006   if rec.na < 'ABC' then k = 1;
  19 c 001C   put list('K=', k);
  20 c 003E   stop;
  21 a 0041 end E49G1;

CODE SIZE = 0041
DATA AREA = 000F
FREE SYMS = 386E
END  COMPILATION
